    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d366">

                <pb facs="0664" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg564"/>

                <head>No. 366.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoppin to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-11-28"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 28, 1879</date>.
                        (Received December 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 113.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 112, of the
                    25th of November, I have now the honor to inclose Lord Salisbury’s formal answer
                    to my inquiry <pb facs="0665" n="565" xml:id="pg565"/> as to when a reply might
                    be expected from him to your instruction, No. 347 to Mr. Welsh in relation to
                    the claims of the Fortune Bay fishermen. You will observe that he explains his
                    delay in this matter by the necessity of a reference to the authorities of
                    Newfoundland.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. J. HOPPIN.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d366-a1.xml" xpointer="d366-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
